{"ticker":"IPCALAB","symbol":"IPCALAB","instrumentId":3022976,"name":"Ipca Laboratories","industry":"NSE-Medical-Generic Drugs","about":"Ipca Laboratories Ltd. is a consumer-driven global pharmaceutical company, providing healthcare solutions for over 60 years across 120+ countries. With a product portfolio of over 350 formulations and 80 APIs, Ipca specializes in pain management, rheumatology, antimalarials, and hair care therapies. The company is one of the world’s largest producers and suppliers of APIs, manufactured at fully-automated facilities that meet the highest regulatory standards from authorities like UK-MHRA and WHO-Geneva. Ipca's leadership in API manufacturing spans over a dozen key APIs globally. the company continues to drive innovation and quality in the pharmaceutical industry.","website":"www.ipca.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:30:45.603Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":1860,"changePct":0.3182136885820663,"week52High":2009.6,"week52Low":1386.2},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹47,189 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹10,479 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"139,537,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"340"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"122,089,162"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.32%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"5.85"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"1.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.12"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.03"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"13%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"32.9"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"30–60"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"14.2%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"45.01"},{"label":"Volume","value":"259,980"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"262,251"},{"label":"Master score","value":"66"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"75"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"77"},{"label":"Group rank","value":"31"},{"label":"Acc/Dis rating","value":"A-"}],"earn